{"user_request": "Please send Owen a concise Slack DM about the handoff for my first quarterly evidence audit of 2028. Ask him to alert me at the appropriate point and include the audit scope he should expect.", "today": "2028-01-01", "tool": "send_slack_dm", "arguments": {"user": "owen", "message": "For my first quarterly evidence audit of 2028, please alert me once the owner-certified four-lane packet is closed and you’ve rechecked the denominator/coverage dates, outcome window, exclusions, reliability evidence, and revenue/forecast treatment. I’ll then do an independent hands-on recheck of one rotating lane across Helio Start, Expansion Assist, pricing-page path quality, or CS auto-nudge controls—without reopening routine source closure or creating a second approval queue."}, "checks": [{"check_id": "riley_074_02", "path": "args", "criterion": "The message asks Owen to alert Riley only after he has closed the relevant routine packet for her first quarterly evidence audit of 2028. It is acceptable to call this a monthly or routine packet and unnecessary to label the packet itself as quarterly or four-lane, provided the audit handoff is clearly post-closure; a request to begin or notify before closure fails.

In the same post-closure audit context, the message states that Riley will select one lane and independently recheck it. This passes without explicitly calling the packet four-lane. It fails if every lane is to be audited, if Owen rather than Riley selects the lane, or if the recheck is not independent.

The expected recheck scope names all of these categories: denominator or coverage dates (either alternative is acceptable), outcome window, exclusions, reliability evidence, revenue treatment, and forecast treatment. Missing or contradicting any category fails.", "value": {"user": "owen", "message": "For my first quarterly evidence audit of 2028, please alert me once the owner-certified four-lane packet is closed and you’ve rechecked the denominator/coverage dates, outcome window, exclusions, reliability evidence, and revenue/forecast treatment. I’ll then do an independent hands-on recheck of one rotating lane across Helio Start, Expansion Assist, pricing-page path quality, or CS auto-nudge controls—without reopening routine source closure or creating a second approval queue."}}]}
